{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgqiZN1EvsYQoBtqQ2ZZV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I couldn't see the code that does the hash check, so this diagnosis is partly an inference.\n\n`AuthService.refreshToken` relies entirely on `sessionService.updateByHash({ id, hash: data.hash }, { hash })` to reject a stale token. The refresh JWT carries `sessionId` and the old `hash`. `JwtRefreshStrategy` only verifies the signature and expiry, so it cannot detect a rotated token. If `updateByHash` doesn't filter on the old hash, or returns the session even when nothing matched, a replayed token still gets a fresh pair. That matches your replay.\n\n`updateByHash` itself wasn't in the snippets. I'd check it first, probably in `src/session/session.service.ts` or the session repository. Its WHERE clause should include both `id` and the old `hash`, and it should return null when no row matches.\n\nI didn't run anything, so none of this is confirmed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4590,"cache_read_input_tokens":791,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4590},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"80a8b04f-f2c0-4485-8ba5-1706efac4dc9","uuid":"ef91c358-6c0a-4d53-bcf9-079727c2ecf0","timestamp":"2026-11-08T15:43:30.886Z","request_id":"req_011CgqiZMnM6ZsD2U8iSXr7x"}
